# =============================================================================
# Batwing canonical .gitattributes asset policy
# =============================================================================
# CANONICAL SOURCE: batwingatx/batwing-specs -> policies/git/gitattributes-canonical
# Do not edit this file in a product repo. Change the canonical copy, then
# re-run the installer. Local drift is what this policy exists to prevent.
#
# Validated by batwing-specs -> tools/validate_gitattributes.py (8 checks).
#
# TWO HARD RULES, both learned the hard way:
#
#   1. .gitattributes has NO inline-comment syntax. A trailing "# note" makes
#      git emit "# is not a valid attribute name". Comments get their own line.
#
#   2. Attributes are LAST-MATCH-WINS, per attribute. Any repo-specific
#      path-anchored rule (e.g. PackageSources/**/*.gltf) MUST be appended
#      BELOW everything in this file, or committed assets silently un-LFS.
#      Append them under the REPO-LOCAL marker at the end.
#
# =============================================================================
# .gitattributes -- Batwing / batlake-strip-test
# Line endings: LF in the repo, native in the working copy.
* text=auto

# Sources borrowed from:
#   - nicolas-fricke/gitattributes-lfs (community LFS canonical set)
#   - Unreal Engine official (Epic Games docs: Using Git LFS with UE)
#   - Unity official (Unity Manual: Version Control)
#   - Reallusion Character Creator 4 / iClone asset formats
#   - Blender / MSFS 2024 SDK / MSFS PackageBuilder
#
# Rationale: shipped asset = tracked asset. Every binary in this list
# routes through Git LFS so devs can `git checkout` the exact source
# artifact that a build shipped, instead of reverse-engineering from
# generator inputs. See batwing/docs/blender-template-conventions.md
# section "Binary asset policy (Git LFS)".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text (never LFS, always diffable)
*.md         text
*.py         text
*.xml        text
*.json       text
*.geojson    text
*.kml        text
*.svg        text
*.cfg        text
*.ini        text
*.toml       text
*.yaml       text
*.yml        text
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bat        text eol=crlf
*.ps1        text eol=crlf
# 3D / DCC source (Blender, Maya, Max, ZBrush, Houdini, C4D)
*.blend      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
